      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this overflows on a Size the host controls. num_bits comes from the MAPD Size field, which process_its_mapd takes as cmd-\u003eraw_cmd[1] \u0026 GENMASK(4, 0) without bounding it against GITS_TYPER.ID_bits, so it can be anything up to 31. nr_ites is an int, so Size 31 shifts by 32, which on arm64 assembles to a shift by 0 and gives nr_ites of 1, and Size 30 shifts into the sign bit and converts to a very large u64 on the multiply below.\n\nThe part that worries me is what happens downstream rather than the shift itself. If num_pages comes out at or below zero, track_pfn iterates zero times, process_its_mapd returns 0, and cwriter_write goes on to submit the MAPD to the real ITS with the host\u0027s itt_addr and nothing pinned, so the ITS writes ITEs into memory we have neither shared nor pinned. Size 31 giving a single page has the same effect for everything past the first page.\n\nCould we bound the Size field against FIELD_GET(GITS_TYPER_IDBITS, gits_typer) before using it, and do the arithmetic in 64 bits, something like: `u64 nr_ites \u003d BIT_ULL(num_bits + 1);`",
      "revId": "d7808e3b5adf0c21af21f22effcae3db4f98cc00",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
