      "writtenOn": "2026-07-30T12:19:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the host can trigger this BUG(). ctlr_write only refuses the transition into enabled while the ITS is not quiescent, so clearing GITS_CTLR.Enabled goes straight through to the hardware. A disabled ITS does not process commands, so GITS_CREADR never advances, and it is not stalled either, so the GITS_CREADR_STALLED check above does not catch it. That leaves disable followed by a GITS_CWRITER write as two MMIO accesses that spin EL2 for 1000 * 100us and then panic the hypervisor.\n\nThe comment reasons about a command that never completes for hardware reasons, which I agree we cannot do much about, but this case is the host picking that state on purpose rather than hardware misbehaving. A hyp panic takes every protected VM down with it, so I do not think it falls under the host being allowed to DoS itself.\n\nCould we refuse to process GITS_CWRITER while GITS_CTLR.Enabled is 0, and return -EBUSY here instead of BUG()? cwriter_write already has the rollback path for a failed submit, so the timeout could just take it.",
      "revId": "d7808e3b5adf0c21af21f22effcae3db4f98cc00",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
